# if you ever archive a version (Zenodo will mint one from a GitHub release).
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PyPSA-India: a workbook-driven power system model for India"
message: "If you use this model or its outputs, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Vikas
    family-names: Jyani
    email: vikas@vasudhaindia.org
    affiliation: Vasudha Foundation
repository-code: "https://github.com/vikasjyani/pypsa-india"
url: "https://vikasjyani.github.io/pypsa-india/"
abstract: >-
  A Snakemake workflow that builds and solves PyPSA power system models of
  India from Excel workbooks. It covers a national five-region scenario and
  one scenario per regional grid, with myopic and perfect-foresight capacity
  expansion, eight typed policy constraints (CO2 caps, renewable purchase
  obligations, monthly capacity-factor profiles, fuel supply ceilings,
  technology phase-out trajectories, reserve margins, corridor transfer limits
  and per-store cycling limits), workbook validation against a single
  component registry, and a post-solve audit of every applied constraint.
keywords:
  - energy system modelling
  - capacity expansion
  - power system planning
  - India
  - PyPSA
  - renewable energy integration
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-17"
